{
  "uid": "wholestory-overview",
  "title": "Whole Story — pipeline",
  "description": "Ordered by what the product promises rather than by what is easy to graph: whether the numbers are arriving at all, then the pipeline, then the two failures that were deliberately kept out of /actuator/health, then latency, and the JVMs last. Provisioned from infra/grafana/dashboards.",
  "tags": [
    "wholestory"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "editable": false,
  "schemaVersion": 41,
  "version": 2,
  "refresh": "10s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Is anything being measured?",
      "description": "Whether Prometheus is reaching each service. This is first on the page because a target that has stopped answering does not make the panels below it fail — they show no data, which looks exactly like no traffic. 'No data' here rather than a red tile means the target is not in the scrape configuration at all, which is a different mistake with the same symptom.",
      "id": 12,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "up{job=\"wholestory\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "value_and_name"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "Not answering",
                  "color": "red",
                  "index": 0
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "Scraped",
                  "color": "green",
                  "index": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "The pipeline",
      "id": 100,
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Events accepted",
      "description": "Pageviews and custom events the collector took. 202 is the only answer a tracked event gets; everything else is counted as a rejection in the panel to the right.",
      "id": 1,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(http_server_requests_seconds_count{service=\"ingest\",uri=\"/api/event\",status=\"202\"}[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "accepted/s",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Events rejected, by reason",
      "description": "The reason a customer's site is not showing data. origin_mismatch and unknown_domain mean a snippet pasted on the wrong domain; rate_limited means one visitor is reporting more than a person can (ADR 0016). Seven reasons exist and all are fixed strings, so this can never grow a series per site.",
      "id": 2,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 5
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (reason) (rate(events_rejected_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{reason}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Crawlers dropped",
      "description": "Counted after the User-Agent is parsed and before anything is stored (D-064). This is the gap between what the collector accepted and what the dashboard will show.",
      "id": 3,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum(rate(events_dropped_total{reason=\"bot\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "bots/s",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "reqps"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Consumer lag",
      "description": "Records behind the head of the topic. Steady near zero is healthy; a climbing line means the processor is not keeping up and the dashboard is showing stale numbers. Spikes right after a deploy are the consumer group rebalancing and are expected.",
      "id": 4,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 13
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max by (service) (kafka_consumer_fetch_manager_records_lag_max)",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "What health deliberately does not say",
      "id": 101,
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 21
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "GeoIP database",
      "description": "Reported here rather than through /actuator/health on purpose (D-059): a missing database costs a location on an event, and must never restart a container that is accepting events perfectly well.",
      "id": 5,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 22
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "geoip_database_loaded",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "text": "Missing",
                  "color": "red",
                  "index": 0
                },
                "1": {
                  "text": "Loaded",
                  "color": "green",
                  "index": 1
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "GeoIP database age",
      "description": "The geoipupdate sidecar refreshes it twice a week. An age that keeps climbing past that means the sidecar has stopped and locations are quietly going stale.",
      "id": 6,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 22
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "geoip_database_age_seconds",
          "legendFormat": "",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Outbox publications not confirmed",
      "description": "The other half of a decision: the mail health indicator was switched off because it dialled SMTP on every check (D-127), and what replaced it was 'a failed send leaves its publication row incomplete'. This is that row. Resubmission runs every five minutes (D-115), so a line that stays above zero for longer than that is a reset mail nobody got, or a site ingest never heard about.",
      "id": 7,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 22
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "outbox_publications_incomplete",
          "legendFormat": "incomplete",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Latency",
      "id": 102,
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 27
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "/api/event",
      "description": "The hot path: the tracker fires this from every visitor's browser. The 1 KB script does not retry, so a request that is slow enough to be abandoned is an event lost for good.",
      "id": 8,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_bucket{service=\"ingest\",uri=\"/api/event\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_bucket{service=\"ingest\",uri=\"/api/event\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Dashboard endpoints, p95 by route",
      "description": "Reporting queries. The breakdown and timeseries routes are the ones that read a whole date range, and the ones a filter makes more expensive (D-103).",
      "id": 9,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 28
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, uri) (rate(http_server_requests_seconds_bucket{service=\"api\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "{{uri}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "The JVMs",
      "id": 103,
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 36
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Heap used",
      "description": "Every container runs with MaxRAMPercentage=75 and ExitOnOutOfMemoryError: a JVM that runs out does not degrade, it dies. This is the panel that says whether there is room for anything else on the host.",
      "id": 10,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 37
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (service) (jvm_memory_used_bytes{area=\"heap\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "unit": "bytes"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Time spent collecting garbage",
      "description": "Seconds of pause per second of wall clock. Read next to the latency panels: a pause is latency nobody wrote any code for.",
      "id": 11,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 37
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "sum by (service) (rate(jvm_gc_pause_seconds_sum[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}}",
          "range": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
